<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">North-West Frontier Province</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/2010">2010</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Khyber Pakhtunkhwa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The North-West Frontier Province was a province created by the British in 1901 from the frontier districts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshawar">Peshawar</a> as its capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">Princely states</a> such as Swat, Dir, Amb and Chitral lay alongside it, and the tribal areas beyond. It became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> in 1947, absorbed the princely states in 1969 and was renamed Khyber Pakhtunkhwa in 2010.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-west-frontier-province.jpg" alt="North-West Frontier Province" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MS05L; Original uploader was Pahari Sahib at en.wikipedia; derivative work by MS05L · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_NWFP.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
